MCrawford wrote:
>
> I see that there used to be a portable nethack

If you mean for a handheld computer that depends on which architecture. 
There are downloads for a lot of architectures off of the
www.nethack.org site and some of them are available in handheld.  There
are plenty of handheld Windows machines and the Windows port is one of
the most commonly downloaded distributions so there may not even need to
be a porting process for yours.

I don't use hand held Windows hosts but I do carry my Nethack
distribution in my pocket on a USB stick that is smaller than any
handheld host I've ever seen.

> (meaning there is no install

By that meaning there isn't any non-portable distribution of Nethack
available that I've seen.  It comes in a wrapper appropriate for the OS
(tar, zip, etc) and it gets unwrapped to be in place.

I have never looked for a Linux RPM module so the "that I've seen" is
not the same as "does not exist".

> or local file/registry writing)

That's a Windows specific term and as such the word "portable" does not
apply to your question.  Windows applications are inherently not
portable for the simple reason they don't also run on VMS, mainframes
and the various UNIX variants.  Nethack runs on all of those and is thus
portable

> However I can't seem to find any leads on a download location or if
> there is even a current build availible.

Start at www.hethack.org.  Follow a bunch of links and read up on it. 
One of the links leads you to distributions all of which do what you
intend.

The word portable doesn't apply in anything like the way you used it. 
The way you used it Nethack has done that for an extremely long time -
The current distribution for Windows has a couple of rarely used options
left out so it fits on a 1.44 MB floppy disk.


